sections := {
        "1": {
            "title": "Purpose",
            "excerpt": "This Departmental Regulation (DR) establishes the United States Department of Agriculture\n   (USDA) policies and procedures for conducting civil rights compliance reviews of all USDA\n   federally conducted and federally assisted programs and employment.",
        },
        "2": {
            "title": "Special Instructions/Cancellations",
            "excerpt": "a.     This DR supersedes Departmental Manual (DM) 4330-001, Procedures for Processing\n          Discrimination Complaints and Conducting Civil Rights Compliance Reviews in USDA\n          Conducted Programs and Activities, dated October 18, 2000.\n\n   b.     This DR is effective immediately and remains in effect until it is superseded or expires.\n   c.   All USDA Mission Areas, agencies, and staff offices will align their policies and\n       procedures with this DR within 6 months of the publicat...",
        },
        "3": {
            "title": "Scope",
            "excerpt": "This DR applies to all USDA personnel responsible for performing compliance reviews of\n  federally conducted and federally assisted programs, and employment.",
        },
        "4": {
            "title": "Policy",
            "excerpt": "a.   Per Federal civil rights laws and USDA civil rights regulations and policies, USDA,\n       Mission Areas, agencies, staff offices, employees, and entities participating in or\n       administering USDA programs are prohibited from discriminating based on race, color,\n       national origin, religion, sex, disability, age, marital status, familial or parental status,\n       income derived from a public assistance program, political beliefs, genetic information,\n       or reprisal or retaliati...",
        },
        "5": {
            "title": "Compliance Methodology",
            "excerpt": "Mission Areas, agencies, staff offices, and OASCR will ensure all equal employment\n  opportunity (EEO) and equal opportunity (EO) programs and activities are conducted,\n  managed, and administered in a non-discriminatory manner. One of the major tools utilized\n  to accomplish this task is the civil rights compliance review. These reviews are systematic,\n  planned examinations conducted to assess and evaluate the policies, procedures, and\n  practices to determine compliance with applicable civil...",
        },
        "6": {
            "title": "Timeframes For The Compliance Review Process",
            "excerpt": "a.   The Mission Area, agency, or staff office will issue a notice to the program or recipient\n       up to 60 calendar days prior to the date that the compliance review activities will\n       commence. The notice will advise the reviewee of the date(s) of the compliance review,\n       the data and information necessary for review prior to the onsite review, and the date on\n       which the requesting Mission Area, agency, or staff office must receive the data and\n       information;\n\n  b.   The...",
        },
        "7": {
            "title": "Types Of Compliance Reviews",
            "excerpt": "a.   Employment Compliance\n\n       EEO Compliance Reviews will be conducted to ensure and determine:\n\n       (1) The level of employee awareness of the EEO laws within their employment. The\n           employee’s awareness should include policy, process, procedure, as well as\n\n\n                                               6\n            “comfort” levels associated with using EEO tools to file a complaint or assess an\n           employee’s satisfaction with the existing conditions and training op...",
        },
        "8": {
            "title": "Oascr Compliance Review Of Mission Areas, Agencies, And Staff",
            "excerpt": "OFFICES\n\n  OASCR is responsible for regularly and systematically monitoring and evaluating its\n  policies, procedures and practices to ensure there is no unlawful discrimination and there is\n  an equal opportunity to participate in agencies’ programs and activities.\n\n  At its discretion, OASCR will conduct compliance reviews of Mission Areas, agencies, and\n  staff offices in accordance with all sections identified above. OASCR may, at its discretion,\n  conduct employment compliance reviews or co...",
        },
        "9": {
            "title": "Enforcement Of Compliance Requirements",
            "excerpt": "The Mission Area, agency, or staff office’s submission of referral of non-compliance, is\n  reviewed by OASCR for completeness and efforts at securing voluntary compliance, and the\n  Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights (ASCR) may:\n\n  a.   Issue a notice of opportunity to the recipient or applicant to request a hearing per 7 CFR\n       Part 15, Nondiscrimination and, if a hearing is requested, arrange for the designation of\n       an administrative law judge to preside over any such hearing; or...",
        },
        "10": {
            "title": "Final Oascr Decision",
            "excerpt": "When OASCR issues a non-compliance notice of findings to the Mission Area, agency, or\n  staff office (final OASCR decision), the notice will cite the corrective actions the Mission\n  Area, agency, or staff office must take to achieve compliance. The notice of findings will\n  include information about the Mission Area, agency, or staff office’s rights and timelines for\n  response.\n\n  OASCR will monitor and evaluate efforts to remedy a non-compliance finding to ensure\n  compliance is consistent wi...",
        },
        "11": {
            "title": "Instructional Manual",
            "excerpt": "OASCR will prepare and disseminate within OASCR and to Mission Area, agency, and staff\n  office civil rights offices manuals, bulletins, and other instructional documents as necessary\n  to implement the provisions of this DR.",
        },
        "12": {
            "title": "Roles And Responsibilities",
            "excerpt": "a.   The Secretary will:\n\n       (1) Provide leadership;\n\n       (2) Set overall civil rights policy and ensure civil rights compliance and enforcement\n           throughout the Department; and\n\n       (3) Ensure the availability of resources adequate to support and carry out a broad range\n           of civil rights compliance and enforcement activities throughout the Department.\n\n  b.   The ASCR will:\n\n       (1) Provide overall leadership, coordination, and direction for USDA civil rights...",
        },
        "13": {
            "title": "Inquiries",
            "excerpt": "All Mission Areas, agencies, and staff offices will direct questions and inquiries regarding\n   this DR to the Center for Civil Rights Operations (CCRO) Compliance Division via email at\n   CCROCompliance@usda.gov.\n\n\n                                            -END-\n\n\n\n\n                                              12\n                                 APPENDIX A\n\n                    ACRONYMS AND ABBREVIATIONS\n\n\nABA         Architectural Barriers Act of 1968\nASCR        Assistant Secretary for Civi...",
        }
}

